WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.299
One order. Typed 3 times.

2
00:00:02.299 --> 00:00:03.393
The quote, the invoice,

3
00:00:03.393 --> 00:00:04.576
the delivery order.

4
00:00:04.576 --> 00:00:05.741
At 40 orders a week,

5
00:00:05.741 --> 00:00:08.479
that is 80 entries nobody needed to type.

6
00:00:09.129 --> 00:00:10.095
I'm an AI voice,

7
00:00:10.095 --> 00:00:12.128
and I speak for Sayed Rashid.

8
00:00:12.128 --> 00:00:14.622
He offers a free 20-minute systems review.

9
00:00:14.622 --> 00:00:16.416
Here is exactly what it is.

10
00:00:16.867 --> 00:00:18.945
You pick one real process: an order,

11
00:00:18.945 --> 00:00:20.841
an invoice, or a stock item.

12
00:00:20.841 --> 00:00:22.892
Then you walk it end to end with Sayed,

13
00:00:22.892 --> 00:00:24.084
on a video call.

14
00:00:24.734 --> 00:00:26.186
You leave with three things.

15
00:00:26.186 --> 00:00:27.630
Where it is typed twice.

16
00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:28.972
Where it sits and waits.

17
00:00:28.972 --> 00:00:31.118
And three fixes, ranked by payoff.

18
00:00:31.118 --> 00:00:33.510
At least one of them needs no purchase.

19
00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:36.542
It is for owners and managers whose

20
00:00:36.542 --> 00:00:38.354
work still runs on spreadsheets,

21
00:00:38.354 --> 00:00:40.050
chat groups and retyping.

22
00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:42.879
It is not for you if you only want a price list.

23
00:00:43.529 --> 00:00:45.697
Why him? Sayed is an ex-auditor.

24
00:00:45.697 --> 00:00:47.675
He has taken 38 systems live,

25
00:00:47.675 --> 00:00:49.319
across 8 industries,

26
00:00:49.319 --> 00:00:52.176
and 91% of those clients are still with him.

27
00:00:53.226 --> 00:00:55.251
It is free. There is nothing to prepare,

28
00:00:55.251 --> 00:00:56.492
and nothing to buy.

29
00:00:56.492 --> 00:00:58.296
There is no pitch unless you ask.

30
00:00:58.296 --> 00:01:00.453
And Sayed takes every call himself.

31
00:01:01.204 --> 00:01:02.500
No time? It is 20 minutes,

32
00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:03.876
and you bring nothing.

33
00:01:03.876 --> 00:01:05.500
Too small? If one process hurts,

34
00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:06.542
that is enough.

35
00:01:06.542 --> 00:01:08.190
Already have software? Good. The

36
00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:10.600
review starts with what you already own.

37
00:01:11.349 --> 00:01:12.163
After you book,

38
00:01:12.163 --> 00:01:14.125
the invite lands in your inbox.

39
00:01:14.125 --> 00:01:14.648
On the day,

40
00:01:14.648 --> 00:01:17.470
you join the call and talk through that one process.

41
00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:20.511
The calendar opens 3 working days ahead,

42
00:01:20.511 --> 00:01:21.927
with 4 slots a day.

43
00:01:21.927 --> 00:01:23.717
If you can see a time, take it.
